<title>UK: UK's MMC clears Cowie /British Bus merger.</title>
<headline>UK's MMC clears Cowie /British Bus merger.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK's Monopolies and Mergers Commission (MMC) has cleared Cowie Group Plc's acquisition of British Bus Group Ltd.</p>
<p>John Taylor, UK Minister for Corporate and Consumer Affairs, said in a statement that he accepted the MMC's conclusion that the acquisition would not operate against the public interest.</p>
<p>Cowie, the UK leasing-to-bus group, had last week reported a bumper 46 percent rise in pre-tax profits to 81.2 million stg in the year to December 31.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4020</p>
</text>
